   "answer": "iPhone 17 — 25W Wireless Charging\n\nYes, the iPhone 17 supports wireless charging up to 25W, but the charger and power adapter must meet the right specifications.\n\nCharging method\n\n\t\n\nMaximum power\n\n\n\n\nMagSafe wireless charging\n\n\t\n\n25W\n\n\n\n\nCompatible Qi2.2 wireless charging\n\n\t\n\n25W\n\n\n\n\nStandard Qi wireless charging\n\n\t\n\n7.5W\n\nImportant: A wireless charger advertised as 25W doesn't necessarily deliver 25W to the iPhone 17. Compatibility with Apple's charging requirements matters.\n\nWhat you need for 25W charging\n\nApple MagSafe Charger or a certified Qi2 25W charger.\n\nA 30W or higher USB-C power adapter for Apple's MagSafe Charger.\n\nProper magnetic alignment.\n\nApple states the iPhone 17 can reach 50% battery in approximately 30 minutes using MagSafe and a 30W adapter. \nApple\n+1\n\nYou can check the official iPhone 17 specifications.\n\nAre you looking to buy a 25W wireless charger, or wondering whether an existing MagSafe/Qi2 charger can deliver 25W to your iPhone 17?"
